    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447">

                <pb facs="0448" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/395: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-18T08:00:00+01:00">September 18,
                            1939—8 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>277. The Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="59" xml:id="d447-f1"/> stated to
                    me this evening that the invasion of Poland by Soviet troops in no way alters
                    Yugoslavia’s position. Although admitting that the Soviet word is of doubtful
                    value he considers that the Soviet guarantee respecting Rumanian territory is
                    helpful. He said he is more than ever convinced that Italy will remain neutral
                    and that Hungary will follow Italy’s lead. He said that the Yugoslav Government
                    is awaiting with much interest the result of the visit to Moscow of the Turkish
                    Foreign Minister<anchor n="60" xml:id="d447-f2"/>
                    <pb facs="0449" n="437" xml:id="pg437"/> particularly in view of Turkey’s
                    arrangements with France and Great Britain.</p>
                <p>The Minister of War<anchor n="61" xml:id="d447-f3"/> informed me today that
                    Rumania will undoubtedly accede to German demands for oil and agricultural
                    products.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
